hadiths[146]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2023","[AI-translation] Darda' who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: Seek out the weak for me, for you are only provided for and granted victory by means of your weak."
"2024","[AI-translation] Zuraqi who said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and said: ""What do you count the people of Badr among you?"" He said: ""From the best of the Muslims."" He said: ""And likewise is whoever of the angels witnessed among us."
"2025","[AI-translation] Hanzaliyyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) passed by a camel whose back had become attached to its belly, so he said: ""Fear Allah regarding these mute animals. Ride them in a fit condition and eat them in a fit condition."
"2026","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah that 'Umar passed by Hassan while he was reciting poetry in the mosque, so he glared at him. He [Hassan] said: ""I used to recite poetry, and in it was one who is better than you."" Then he turned to Abu Hurayrah and said: ""I adjure you by Allah! Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: 'Reply on my behalf. O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit'?"
"2027","[AI-translation] From Umm Kabshah, a woman from Quda'ah: that she asked permission from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) to go on a military expedition with him. He said: ""No."" She said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I treat the wounded and attend to the sick."" He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Sit, lest the people talk that Muhammad goes on a military expedition with a woman."
"2028","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) gave testament regarding three things, and he said: ""Expel the polytheists from the Arabian Peninsula, and honor the delegations as I used to honor them."" Then he said: Ibn 'Abbas said: ""And he remained silent about the third, or he said: 'And I forgot it.'"
"2029","[AI-translation] From Abu 'Ubaydah who said: The last thing the Prophet (peace be upon him) spoke was: ""Expel the Jews of the Hijaz and the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula, and know that the worst of people are those who take the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"2030","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""When the land becomes lush, dismount from your mounts and give them their right to pasturage, and when the land becomes barren, proceed upon them. And upon you is night travel, for the land is folded up by the night."
"2031","[AI-translation] From Uqbah bin Aamir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you intend to go to battle, buy a dark bay horse with a blaze, white markings, and a completely white right leg, for you will gain spoils and be safe."
"2032","[AI-translation] From Sakhr bin Eilah: Some people from Banu Sulaim fled from their land when Islam came, so I took it. Then they embraced Islam and disputed with me over it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He returned it to them and said: When a man embraces Islam, he is more entitled to his land and property."
"2033","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, he said: When you leave your house, pray two rak'ahs, which will protect you from the evil of going out, and when you enter your house, pray two rak'ahs, which will protect you from the evil of entering."
"2034","[AI-translation] Rabi, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, and asked him, and he ordered for me a few camels. Then he said to me: When you return to your home, instruct them to feed their livestock well, and instruct them to trim their fingernails, and not to damage the udders of their livestock with them when they milk."
"2035","[AI-translation] Aas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, that he said: When the (treasures) of Persia and Rome are opened for you, what kind of people will you be? Abdur-Rahman bin Awf said: We will say as Allah has commanded us. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Or otherwise, you will compete, then envy one another, then turn your backs on one another, then hate one another, or something like that, then you will set out among the poor of the Muhajirun and place some of them upon the necks of others."
"2036","[AI-translation] Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: When they are three (on a journey), one of them should lead them in prayer, and the most entitled of them to lead is the one who recites the Quran best."
"2037","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: When you pass by a land where a nation was destroyed, hasten your journey."
"2038","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: When the fierce battles occur, Allah will dispatch an army from the Mawali (from Damascus); they are the noblest of the Arabs in horsemanship and the best in weaponry; Allah will support the religion through them."
"2039","[AI-translation] From Muadh bin Anas, raised to the Prophet: Ride these mounts while they are sound, and leave them while they are sound, and do not use them as chairs."
"2040","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, passed by some people who were shooting arrows and said: Shoot, (O sons of Ismail), for your father was an archer."
"2041","[AI-translation] soldiers among his Companions gathered to him and formed rows for him, and said: ""We expose ourselves to the supplications of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" They said: ""The journey has become strenuous upon us, and the distance has grown long."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said to them: ""Seek help through brisk walking (an-nasl), for it cuts the land for you and you become light for it."" He said: ""So we did it, and we became light for it, and what we used to experience (of fatigue) went away."
"2042","Sahl ibn al-Ḥanẓaliyyah narrated that they traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) on the day of Ḥunayn. They traveled extensively until it was evening. The time for prayer arrived while they were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). A horseman came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I went ahead of you until I climbed such-and-such mountain, and there I saw Hawāzin on their mounts with their women, children, and sheep gathered at Ḥunayn."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) smiled and said: ""That is the spoils of the Muslims tomorrow, if Allah wills."" Then he said: ""Who will guard us tonight?"" Anas ibn Abī Marthad al-Ghanawī said: ""I will, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Then ride."" So he rode his horse and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Face this mountain pass until you are at its top, and do not let us be taken by surprise from your direction tonight."" When morning came, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) went out to his place of prayer and prayed two rakʿahs. Then he said: ""Did you perceive your horseman?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We did not perceive him."" The call to prayer (iqāmah) was made, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prayed while turning towards the mountain pass until he finished his prayer and gave the salām. He said: ""Rejoice, for your horseman has come to you."" We looked through the trees in the mountain pass, and there he was, coming until he stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and gave salām. He said: ""I went until I was at the top of this mountain pass where the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded me. When morning came, I overlooked both mountain passes and saw no one."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Did you dismount tonight?"" He said: ""No, except to pray or relieve myself."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: ""You have earned (Paradise), so there is no blame on you if you do not work after it."""
"2043","[AI-translation] From Qaza'ah who said: Ibn Umar sent me on an errand, and he said: ""Come, so that I may bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) bade me farewell when he sent me on an errand of his. He said: 'I entrust Allah with your religion, your trustworthiness, and the sealing of your deeds.'"
"2044","[AI-translation] Khatmi who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), when he intended to bid the army farewell, would say: ""I entrust Allah with your religion, your trustworthiness, and the sealing of your deeds."
"2045","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace be upon him), whenever he bade anyone farewell, would say: ""I entrust Allah with your religion, your trustworthiness, and the sealing of your deeds."
"2046","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family): ""The anger of Allah intensified against a people who did this to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family)"" – and at that time he was pointing to his front teeth – ""The anger of Allah intensified against a man whom the Messenger of Allah kills in the path of Allah."
"2047","[AI-translation] Juhani who said: ""I left al-Sham for al-Madinah on Friday and entered upon Umar bin al-Khattab. He said: 'When did you insert your two leather socks onto your feet?' I said: 'On Friday.' He said: 'Did you take them off?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'You have hit the Sunnah.'"
"2048","[AI-translation] Khudri, raised to the Prophet: ""The best of Jihad in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection are those who are cast into the ranks and do not turn their faces until they are killed. They will be rolling about in the highest chambers of Paradise; your Lord looks at them. Indeed, your Lord, when He laughs at a people, there is no reckoning upon them."
"2049","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: ""The best of Jihad is a word of justice (and in a narration: of truth) before an unjust ruler."" (This is also reported from the hadith of Abu Said al-Khudri, Abu Umamah, Tariq bin Shihab, and Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them, and al-Zuhri as mursal.)"
"2050","[AI-translation] From Amr bin Abasah, raised to the Prophet: ""The best of Jihad is he whose steed is hamstrung and whose blood is shed."
"2051","[AI-translation] Khudri that a man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and said: ""Which of the people is best?"" He said: ""The best of the people"" - and in a narration: ""The best of the people is a man who strives in the path of Allah with his wealth and his self, then a believer in a mountain pass among the mountain passes, worshipping Allah, his Lord, and sparing the people from his evil."
"2052","Abdullah ibn Ja'far reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated me behind him on his mount one day and whispered to me a hadith that I shall not narrate to anyone. The most beloved thing for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to screen himself with for his needs was a target or a grove of palm trees. He entered a garden belonging to a man of the Ansar, and there was a camel. When it saw the Prophet ﷺ, it groaned and its eyes shed tears. The Prophet ﷺ came to it and wiped its forehead and its hump, so it became calm. He said: ""Who is the master of this camel? To whom does this camel belong?"" A young man of the Ansar came and said: ""It is mine, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Do you not fear Allah concerning this beast which Allah has given you possession of? For it has complained to me that you starve it and overwork it."""
"2053","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, passed by a man who had placed his foot on the side of a sheep while he was sharpening his blade, and it was looking at him. He said: ""Could you not have done this before?! Do you want to make it die two deaths?!"
"2054","[AI-translation] From Fadalah who said: A man approached and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, peace be upon you, what is the deed nearest to Jihad?"" He said: ""The deed nearest to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Jihad in the path of Allah, and nothing rivals it except (one who is like this,"" and the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, gestured to a man standing who does not cease from standing or fasting.)"
"2055","[AI-translation] and perhaps he did not raise it (to the Prophet)—who said: ""Shall I not inform you of a night better than the Night of Decree? A guard who stood guard in a land of fear, who perhaps may not return to his family."
"2056","[AI-translation] Tufayl who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, laughed until his laughter was profound. Then he said: ""Do you not ask me what I laughed at?"" We said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What did you laugh at?"" He said: ""I saw people from my Ummah being driven to Paradise in chains which they disliked."" We said: ""Who are they?"" He said: ""People from the non-Arabs (al-Ajam), whom the emigrants (al-Muhajirun) take captive and enter them into Islam."
"2057","[AI-translation] From Sulayman ibn Surad who said: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, when he drove the Confederates (meaning the Day of the Trench) away: ""Now (and in a narration: today) we invade them (meaning: the polytheists of Makkah who were defeated in the Battle of the Trench) and they do not invade us (we march towards them)."
"2058","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Umar that he instructed a man, when he took to his bed, to say: ""O Allah, (You) created my soul and You take it back. To You belongs its death and its life. If You give it life, protect it, and if You cause it to die, forgive it. O Allah, I ask You for well-being."" A man said to him: ""Did you hear this from Umar?"" He replied: ""From one better than Umar, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family."
"2059","Ziyad ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah narrated: My father informed me that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Al-Hurmuzan: ""Since you have been spared, then advise me."" This was because he had said to him: ""Speak, there is no harm,"" so he granted him safety. Al-Hurmuzan said: ""Yes, Persia today is a head and two wings."" He asked: ""Where is the head?"" He said: ""Nahavand, with Bendar."" He said: ""Then with him are the Asawira of Kisra and the people of Isfahan."" He asked: ""Where are the two wings?"" Al-Hurmuzan mentioned a place which I have forgotten. Al-Hurmuzan said: ""Cut off the two wings and you will weaken the head."" Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: ""You lie, O enemy of Allah! Rather, I will aim for the head, and Allah will cut it off; and when Allah cuts it off from me, the two wings will be cut off from me."" Then Umar intended to march to it himself. They said: ""We remind you of Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, that you march yourself to the Persians (Al-Ajam); for if you are killed, there will be no order for the Muslims. But send the armies."" He said: So he sent the people of Madinah, and he sent among them Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he sent the Muhajirun and the Ansar. And he wrote to Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari: ""March with the people of Basrah."" And he wrote to Hudhayfah ibn Al-Yaman: ""March with the people of Kufah, until you all gather at Nahavand together. When you have gathered, your commander is An-Nu'man ibn Muqrin Al-Muzani.""فَلَمَا اجْتَمَعُوا بنهاوند أَرْسَل إِلَيْهِم بُنْدَار (العلج) أَن أَرْسِلُوا إِلَيْنَا يَا مَعْشَر الْعَرَب رَجُلًا مِنْكُم نُكَلِّمُهُ، فَاخْتَار النَّاسُ الْمُغِيَرة بن شعبة، قال أَبِيْ: فَكَأَنِّي أَنْظُرُ إِلَيْه رَجُلٌ طويلٌ، أَشْعَثَ أعورَ، فَأَتَاهُ، فَلَمَّا رَجَعَ إِلَيْنَا سَأَلْنَاهُ؟ فَقَال لَنا: إِنِّي وَجَدْتُ الْعَلَج قَد اسْتَشَار أَصْحَابه في أَيِّ شَيْءٍ تَأْذَنُون لِهَذَا العربي؟ أَبَشَارَتُنَا وَبَهْجَتُنَا وَمُلْكُنَا؟ أَوْ نَتَقَشَّفُ لَهُ، فَنَزْهَدُهُ عَمَّا في أَيْدِيَنَا؟ فَقَالُوا: بَل نَأْذَن لَه بِأَفْضَل ما يَكُون من الشَّارَة والعدة، فَلَمَّا رَأَيْتُهُم رَأَيْتُ تِلْكَ الحِرَاب، وَالدَّرَق يَلْمَعُ مِنْهُ البَصَر، وَرَأَيْتُهُم قِيَامًا عَلَى رأسه، وَإِذَا هُو عَلَى سَرِيرٍ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ، وَعَلَى رَأْسِهِ التَّاجُ، فَمَضَيْتُ كَمَا أَنَا، وَنَكَسْتُ رَأْسِي لِأَقْعُد مَعَه عَلَى السرير، قال: فَدُفِعْتُ وَنُهِرْتُ، فَقُلْتُ إِن الرُّسُل لَا يُفْعَلُ بِهْم هَذا، فَقَالُوا لِي : إِنَّمَا أَنْتَ كَلْبٌ أَتَقْعُد مَعَ الْمَلِكِ؟!، فَقُلْت: لَأَنَا أَشْرَفُ في قَوْمِي مِنْ هَذَا فِيْكُمْ، قَالَ : فَانْتَهَرَنِي، وَقَالَ: اِجْلِسْ، فَجَلَسْتُ، فَتُرْجِمَ لِي قَولُه؟ فَقَال: يَا مَعْشَرَ الْعَرَبِ! إِنَّكُم كُنْتُم أَطْوَل النَّاس جُوْعًا، وَأَعْظَم النَّاس شَقَاءً، وَأَقْذَرَ النَّاس قَذَرًا، وَأَبْعَد النَّاس دارًا، وأَبْعَدَهُ مِنْ كُلِّ خَيْرٍ، وَمَا كَان مَنَعَنِي أَن آمُر هَذِه الأَسَاوِرَةِ حَوْلِي، أَنْ يَنْتَظِمُوْكُمْ بِالنِّشَابِ، إِلَا تَنْجِيْسًا لِجِيَفِكُمْ لِأَنَّكُم أَرْجَاسٌ، فَإِن تَذْهَبُوا يُخَلّٰي عَنْكُمْ، وَإِنْ تَأْبُوا نُبَوِّئُكُمْ مَصَارِعَكُمْ،""Translation: When they gathered at Nahavand, Bendar (the Alaj - a derogatory term for a non-Arab/Persian noble) sent to them saying: ""Send to us, O company of Arabs, a man from among you that we may speak to him."" The people chose Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. My father said: ""It is as if I see him now, a tall man, disheveled, one-eyed. He went to him. When he returned to us, we asked him. He said to us: 'I found the Alaj had consulted his companions: ""In what do you permit this Arab? Is it in our good tidings, our joy, and our kingdom? Or do we endure hardship for him, so that he may renounce what is in our hands?"" They said: ""Rather, we permit him with the best possible insignia and equipment."" When I saw them, I saw those spears and shields, dazzling the sight. I saw them standing at his head, and there he was on a bed of gold, and on his head was the crown. I walked on as I was, and lowered my head to sit with him on the bed. He said: I was pushed and rebuked. I said: ""Messengers are not treated like this."" They said to me: ""You are but a dog; do you sit with the King?!"" I said: ""I am more noble among my people than this one is among you."" He rebuked me and said: ""Sit."" So I sat. His speech was translated for me. He said: ""O company of Arabs! You were the most hungry of people, the most wretched of people, the filthiest of people, the farthest of people from home, and the farthest from all good. Nothing prevented me from ordering these Asawira around me to pepper you with arrows, except the defilement of your corpses, for you are impure. If you leave, we will leave you alone; and if you refuse, we will assign you your places of slaughter.""'""قال الْمُغِيَرة : فَحَمَدْتُ الله وَأَثْنَيْتُ عَلَيْهِ، وَقُلْتُ : وَالله ما أَخْطَأَتَ مِنْ صِفَتِنَا وَنَعْتِنَا شَيْئًا، إِنْ كُنَّا لَأَبْعَد النَّاس دَارًا وَأَشَدّ النَّاس جُوعًا وَأَعْظَم النَّاس شَقَاءً وَأَبْعَد النَّاس من كُل خَيْرٍ حَتَّى بَعَثَ الله إِلَيْنَا رَسُوْلًا، فَوَعَدَنَا بِالنَّصْر في الدُّنْيَا وَالْجَنَّة في الآخرة، فَلَم نَزَلْ نَتَعَرَّفُ مِنْ رَبِّنَا مُذْ جَاءَنَا رَسُولُه صلی اللہ علیہ وآلہ وسلم الفَلاح، وَالنَّصْرَ، حَتَّى أَتَيْنَاكُمْ، وَإِنَّا وَالله نَرَى لَكُم مُلْكًا وَعَيْشًا لَا نَرْجِعُ إِلَى ذَلِكَ الشَّقَاءِ أَبَدًا، حَتَّى نَغْلِبَكُمْ عَلَى مَا فِي أَيْدِيْكُمْ، أَو نُقْتُلَ في أَرْضِكُمْ، فَقَال : أَمَّا الأعور، فَقَد صَدَقَكُم الَّذِي في نفسه، فَقُمْتُ مِنْ عِنْدِهِ، وَقَد وَالله أرْعَبْتُ الْعَلْج جهدي، فَأَرْسَل إِلَيْنَا الْعَلْج إِمَّا أَن تَعْبُرُوا إِلَيْنَا بِنَهَاوَنْد، وَإِمَّا أَنْ نَعْبُرَ إِلَيْكُمْ، فَقَال النُّعْمَان : اُعْبُرُوا، فَعَبَرْنَا قَالَ أَبِي : فَلَم أَر كَالْيَوْم قَطُ، إِن الْعُلُوج يجيئون، كَأَنَّهُم جِبَال الحَدِيْد، وَقَدْ تَوَاثَقُوا أَنْ لَا يَفِرُّوا مِنَ العَرَبِ، وَقَد قُرن بَعْضُهُم إِلَى بَعْضٍ، حَتَّى كَان سَبْعَةٌ في قران، وَأَلْقَوْا حَسَك الْحَدِيد خَلْفَهُمْ، وَقَالُوا : من فَر مِنَّا عقره حَسَك الحديد، فَقَال الْمُغِيَرة بن شُعُبَة حِين رَأَى كَثْرَتَهُم : لَم"""
"2060","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""The Asharis, when they run short of provisions during a raid, or the food of their dependents in Madinah becomes scarce, they gather whatever they have in one cloth, then divide it among themselves in one vessel equally. They are of me and I am of them."
"2061","From Humayd (meaning: Ibn Hilal) who said: There was a man from Al-Tufawah whose route passed by us. He came to the tribe and narrated to them, saying: ""I arrived in Medina with a caravan of ours and we sold our merchandise (the original manuscript reads 'our sale'). Then I said: 'I will surely go to this man so that I may bring back news of him to those after me.' He said: So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him showing me a house. He said: 'A woman used to live in it (meaning a house in Medina). She went out in a military expedition of the Muslims and left behind twelve she-goats of hers, and her spindle with which she used to spin. He said: Then she lost a she-goat from her flock and her spindle. She said: ""O Lord, You have guaranteed for whoever goes out in Your path that You will protect his property, and I have lost a she-goat from my flock and my spindle, and I beseech You for my she-goat and my spindle."" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began mentioning the intensity of her beseeching her Lord, Blessed and Exalted. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then her she-goat was found in the morning, and another like it, and her spindle, and another like it, and those (the original twelve). So go to her and ask her if you wish.'"""
"2062","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""The first of people against whom judgment will be pronounced on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who died a martyr. He will be brought forth and Allah will make known to him His favors and he will recognize them. He will say: 'What did you do about them?' He will say: 'I fought for You until I died a martyr.' He will say: 'You have lied, but you fought that it might be said: ""He is courageous."" And so it was said.' Then he will be ordered to be dragged along on his face until he is cast into Hellfire.And [another will be] a man who acquired knowledge and taught it and recited the Qur'an. He will be brought forth and Allah will make known to him His favors and he will recognize them. He will say: 'What did you do about them?' He will say: 'I acquired knowledge and taught it and recited the Qur'an for Your sake.' He will say: 'You have lied, but you acquired knowledge that it might be said: ""He is a scholar,"" and you recited the Qur'an that it might be said: ""He is a reciter."" And so it was said.' Then he will be ordered to be dragged along on his face until he is cast into Hellfire.And [another will be] a man whom Allah made rich and gave him all kinds of wealth. He will be brought forth and Allah will make known to him His favors and he will recognize them. He will say: 'What did you do about them?' He will say: 'I left no path in which You like money to be spent without spending in it for Your sake.' He will say: 'You have lied, but you did it that it might be said: ""He is generous."" And so it was said.' Then he will be ordered to be dragged along on his face until he is cast into Hellfire."""
"2063","Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), said: ""When Makkah became constricted for us, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) were harmed and tested, and they saw the affliction and trial befalling them in their religion, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) could not ward that off from them — while the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was in a position of protection from his people and his uncle, nothing of what he disliked reaching him from what befell his companions — the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to them: 'Indeed, in the land of Abyssinia there is a king under whom no one is wronged, so go to his land until Allah makes for you a way out and relief from what you are in.' So we went out to it in groups until we gathered there, and we settled in the best of abodes with the best of neighbors; we were secure in our religion and did not fear any injustice from him."""
"2064","[AI-translation] Bara ibn Azib: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""If you are attacked by night, let your watchword be: 'Ha Mim, they shall not be helped' (la yunsarun)."
"2065","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: ""Which Jihad is best?"" He said: ""That you strive against your soul and your desires in the cause of Allah."
"2066","[AI-translation] Saidi: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, went out on the day of Uhud until, when he passed Thaniyat al-Wada, he encountered a rough-looking detachment. He said: ""Who are these?"" They said: ""This is Abdullah ibn Ubayy (ibn Salul) with six hundred of his clients from the Jews of Qaynuqa, and they are the kinsfolk of Abdullah ibn Salam."" He said: ""Have they embraced Islam?"" They said: ""No, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Tell them to go back, for we do not seek help from polytheists against polytheists."
"2067","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""What do you count as a martyr?"" They said: ""The one who fights in the path of Allah until he is killed."" He said: ""Then the martyrs in my Ummah would be few. The slain in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one who dies of plague in the path of Allah is a martyr, the drowned in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one thrown off his mount in the path of Allah is a martyr, and the one who dies of pleurisy in the path of Allah is a martyr."" Muhammad (meaning Ibn Ishaq) said: al-majnub means the one suffering from pleurisy (sahib al-janib)."
"2068","Buraydah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on one of his military expeditions. When he returned, a black slave girl came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I vowed that if Allah returned you safely, I would beat the duff before you and sing."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""If you vowed, then beat it; otherwise, do not."" So she began to beat it. Then Abu Bakr entered while she was beating it, then ʿAlī entered while she was beating it, then ʿUthmān entered while she was beating it, then ʿUmar entered and she threw the duff beneath her buttocks and sat upon it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed, Satan fears you, O ʿUmar. I was sitting while she was beating it; then Abu Bakr entered while she was beating it, then ʿAlī entered while she was beating it, then ʿUthmān entered while she was beating it, but when you entered, O ʿUmar, she threw the duff."""
"2069","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: The believer certainly exhausts his devils just as one of you exhausts his riding camel during a journey."
"2070","[AI-translation] From Ka'b ibn Malik, that he said to the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has revealed regarding poetry what He has revealed."" He said: ""The believer strives with his sword and his tongue. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, it is as if what you shoot at them with is a volley of arrows."
"2071","[AI-translation] From Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, that some men from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to one another: ""Hijrah has ceased."" They differed regarding that. He said: So I went to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Some people are saying that Hijrah has ceased."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Hijrah does not cease as long as there is Jihad."
"2072","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Allah the Almighty has undertaken for the one who goes out in His cause, not being driven out except for jihad in My cause and belief in Me and affirmation of My messengers, that he is guaranteed by Me that I will admit him to Paradise or return him to his dwelling from which he went out, having obtained what he attained of reward or spoils. And by Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad! There is no wound received in the cause of Allah except that it will come on the Day of Resurrection in the same condition as when it was received; its color the color of blood, and its scent the scent of musk. And by Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad! Were it not that it would be difficult for the Muslims, I would never have stayed behind from any expedition fighting in the cause of Allah. But I do not find the means to carry them, and they do not find the means to follow me, and it would be hard on their souls to stay behind after me. And by Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad! I would love to fight in the cause of Allah and be killed, then fight and be killed, then fight and be killed."
"2073","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah who said: I came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, while he was in a red dome. 'Abd al-Malik said: Of leather, with around forty men. He said: ""You will have lands opened unto you, you will be victorious, and you will succeed. Whoever among you lives to see that, let him fear Allah, enjoin good, forbid evil, and uphold ties of kinship. Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And the likeness of the one who aids his people in falsehood is like a camel that has fallen into a well, being pulled out by its tail."
"2074","[AI-translation] From Yahya ibn Sa'id that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was seen wiping the face of his horse with his cloak. He was asked about that, and he said: ""I was rebuked tonight regarding horses."
"2075","[AI-translation] From Abu Rafi', who said: Quraysh sent me to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family. When I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, Islam was cast into my heart. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I will never return to them ever again."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""I do not break a pledge, nor do I detain envoys, but return. If what is in your heart now persists, then return."
"2076","[AI-translation] Khudri, that a man came to him and said: ""Counsel me."" He said: ""You have asked about what one before you asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family. I counsel you to fear Allah, for it is the head of all things. And adhere to Jihad, for it is the monasticism of Islam. And adhere to the remembrance of Allah and the recitation of the Qur'an, for it is your spirit in the heaven and your remembrance on the earth."
"2077","[AI-translation] From Sahl ibn Hunayf, raised to the Prophet: With the first drop of blood spilled from a martyr, all his sins are forgiven except debt."
"2078","[AI-translation] From Hamzah ibn 'Amr: That he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, about fasting during a journey. He said: ""Whichever of that is easier for you, then do it."
"2079","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: Beware of taking the backs of your mounts as pulpits, for Allah, Exalted is He, has only subjected them to you to convey you to a land you would not have reached except with great strain to your souls. And He has made the earth for you, so fulfill your needs upon it."
"2080","From Abu Taybah: Shurahbil ibn al-Mustat called for Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami and said: ""O Ibn Abasah! Will you narrate to me a hadith that you heard yourself from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, in which there is no addition, no lie, and you do not narrate it from someone else who heard it other than you?"" He said: ""Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say:'Any man who shoots an arrow in the cause of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and it reaches its target, whether missing or hitting, for him is a reward equal to that of freeing a slave from the descendants of Ismail.And any man who grays a hair in the cause of Allah, it will be a light for him.And any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, every limb of the freed person will ransom a limb of the freer from the Fire.And any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, every limb of the freed woman will ransom a limb of the freer from the Fire.And any Muslim man who presents to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, from his own loins three children who did not reach the age of puberty, or a woman [who does the same], they will be a shield for him from the Fire.And any man who rises for ablution intending prayer, and perfects the ablution in its proper places, he will be secure from every sin or offense he has committed. Then if he stands for prayer, Allah will raise him by it a degree; and if he sits, he sits secure.'"""
"2081","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), marfu'an: While a man was walking along a road, he was overcome by thirst. He found a well, so he descended into it and drank. When he came out, there was a dog panting, eating the damp earth out of thirst. The man said, ""This dog has suffered from thirst just as I have suffered."" So he descended into the well, filled his leather sock, held it with his mouth, and climbed up. He gave the dog to drink, so Allah thanked him and forgave him. They said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there a reward for us even in animals?"" He said, ""In every moist liver there is a reward."
"2082","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), marfu'an: While a dog was circling a well, almost dying of thirst, a prostitute from among the prostitutes of Banu Isra'il saw him. She took off her leather sock, drew water with it, and gave him to drink. She was forgiven for that."
"2083","[AI-translation] Narrated Nafi' bin 'Utbah bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""You will fight in the Arabian Peninsula, and Allah will conquer it for you; then Persia, and Allah will conquer it for you; then the Romans, and Allah will conquer it for you; then the Dajjal, and Allah will conquer him for you."
"2084","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Three supplications are answered, there is no doubt in them: the supplication of a parent, the supplication of a traveler, and the supplication of the oppressed."
"2085","On the authority of Abu al-Darda', from the Prophet ﷺ who said: ""There are three whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves; He laughs to them and rejoices over them: The one who, when a detachment is exposed, fights behind it with his life for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so either he is killed, or Allah grants him victory and suffices him; then Allah says: 'Look at My servant, how he patiently offered his life for Me.' And the one who has a beautiful wife and a soft, comfortable bed, then he rises from the night — leaving his desire — so he remembers Me and converses intimately with Me, though if he wished he could have slept. And the one who is on a journey and has a company with him, so they stay up late and exert themselves, then they sleep, so he stands at the pre-dawn time in ease or hardship."""
"2086","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas: A man left Khaybar, and two men followed him. Another man was following them, saying, ""Go back."" He caught up with them and turned them back. Then (he caught up with the first man) and said, ""These two are devils. I persisted with them until I turned them away from you. When you come to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), convey peace to the Messenger of Allah, and inform him that we are gathering our charity. If it were permissible for him, we would have sent it to him."" He said: When the man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), he told him, and he forbade seclusion at that time."
"2087","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""The best of companions are four, the best of squadrons are four hundred, and the best of armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand will not be overcome due to paucity."
"2088","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), marfu'an: The best of people during trials is a man holding the reins of his horse—or he said: the halter of his horse—behind the enemies of Allah, frightening them and they frightening him; or a man secluded in his desert, fulfilling the right of Allah that is upon him."
"2089","[AI-translation] Narrated Umm Mubashshir, reaching with it the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), who said: ""The best of people in station is a man upon the back of his horse, frightening the enemy and they frightening him."
"2090","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Amr, marfu'an: The single rider is a devil, two riders are two devils, and three are a riding party."
"2091","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah bin 'Amr, elevated to the Prophet: The lone rider is a shaytan, and two riders are two shaytans, and three are a rakb."
"2092","[AI-translation] The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Travel and you will become healthy, and carry out military expeditions and you will become independent."" This is reported from the hadith of Abu Hurairah, Ibn 'Amr, Ibn 'Abbas, and Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with them, and from Zaid bin Aslam as a mursal hadith."
"2093","Talq ibn Habib al-Basri narrated that Abu Taliq told them: His wife, Umm Taliq, came to him and said: ""The Hajj season has arrived, O Abu Taliq."" He had a camel and a she-camel; he would perform Hajj on the she-camel and go on military expeditions on the camel. She asked him to give her the camel to perform Hajj on it. He said: ""Do you not know that I have dedicated it for the cause of Allah?"" She said: ""Indeed, Hajj is of the cause of Allah, so give it to me, may Allah have mercy on you."" He said: ""I do not wish to give it to you."" She said: ""Then give me your she-camel and you perform Hajj on the camel."" He said: ""I will not prefer you with it over myself."" She said: ""Then give me from your provisions."" He said: ""I have nothing surplus beyond my needs and my family's needs to take with me or leave for you."" She said: ""Indeed, if you gave it to me, Allah would replace it for you."" He said: ""When I refused her, she said: 'When you come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, convey my greetings of peace to him and inform him of what I said to you.'"" He said: ""So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, conveyed her greetings of peace to him, and informed him of what Umm Taliq had said."" He said: ""Umm Taliq spoke the truth. If you had given her the camel, it would have been in the cause of Allah; if you had given her your she-camel, it would have been in the cause of Allah, and you would have been in the cause of Allah; if you had given her from your provisions, Allah would have replaced it for you."" He said: ""And she asks you, O Messenger of Allah, what equals Hajj (with you)?"" He said: ""An Umrah in Ramadan."""
"2094","[AI-translation] Arqam bin Abi al-Arqam, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said on the day of Badr: ""Gather whatever spoils you have with you."" Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi raised the sword of Ibn 'A'idh al-Marzuban, and al-Arqam bin Abi al-Arqam recognized it and said: ""Give it to me, O Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him."" So he gave it to him."
"2095","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah bin 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, elevated to the Prophet: A woman was punished concerning a cat she confined until it died, and she entered the Fire because of it. She neither fed it nor gave it water when she confined it, nor did she leave it to eat from the vermin of the earth."
"2096","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah bin 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""What is to be conquered for my Ummah after me was presented to me, and it pleased me."" So Allah, Exalted be He, revealed: ""And the Hereafter is better for you than the first [life]"" (Ad-Duha: 4), up to His saying: ""And you will be pleased"" (5). Allah gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces of pearl, their dust being musk, in every palace is what is fitting for him."
"2097","[AI-translation] From Abu Fatimah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Upon you is emigration, for it has no equal. Upon you is fasting, for it has no equal. Upon you is prostration, for you do not prostrate a prostration to Allah except that Allah raises you a degree by it and removes a sin from you by it."
"2098","[AI-translation] Samit, elevated: Upon you is Jihad in the path of Allah, Blessed and Exalted be He, for it is a gate from the gates of Paradise by which Allah removes worry and grief."
"2099","[AI-translation] From Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Upon you is traveling by night, for the earth is folded by night."
"2100","[AI-translation] From Mus'ab bin Sa'd (bin Abi Waqqas), from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Upon you is archery, for it is the best of your games."
"2101","[AI-translation] From Jabir, who said: Some people complained to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, about walking. He called for them and said: ""Upon you is brisk walking."" So we walked briskly and found it lighter upon us."
"2102","[AI-translation] Bara', Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man from the Ansar wearing a helmet of iron came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, shall I fight or embrace Islam?"" He said: ""(No, rather) embrace Islam, then fight."" So he embraced Islam, then fought and was killed. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""He did little but was rewarded much."
"2103","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurairah, marfu': Al-'Arrafah (soothsaying), its beginning is blame, its end is regret, and the punishment on the Day of Resurrection."
"2104","Aslam Abu Imran said: We went on an expedition from Medina intending Constantinople (and over the people of Egypt was Uqbah ibn Amir), and over the army was Abdur-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Al-Walid. The Romans had their backs pressed against the city wall. Then a man from among us charged at the enemy, and the people said: ""Hold on, hold on! There is no god but Allah, he is throwing himself into destruction with his own hands."" Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari said: ""You interpret this verse only thus: 'If a man charges to fight seeking martyrdom or to prove himself,' but this verse was revealed concerning us, the Ansar, when Allah supported His Prophet and made Islam manifest. We said secretly among ourselves, away from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): 'Come, let us stay with our wealth and improve it.' So Allah the Exalted revealed: 'And spend in the way of Allah and do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction.' So throwing yourselves with your own hands into destruction means that we stay with our wealth and improve it and abandon jihad."" Abu Imran said: Abu Ayyub did not cease to strive in the way of Allah until he was buried in Constantinople."
"2105","[AI-translation] Narrated from Mu'adh bin Jabal, marfu': Battle is of two types. As for the one who seeks the Face of Allah, obeys the Imam, spends his best wealth, and avoids corruption, then his sleeping and his waking are all reward. As for the one who fights out of pride, showing off, and to be heard, disobeys the Imam, and spreads corruption in the land, he will not return empty-handed."
"2106","[AI-translation] Narrated from Rabah bin Rabee', who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, on a military expedition, and he saw the people gathered around something. He sent a man and said: ""See what these people have gathered around."" He came and said: ""Around a slain woman."" He said: ""She was not one to fight."" He (Rabah) said: And Khalid bin Al-Waleed was at the vanguard, so he sent a man and said: ""Tell Khalid not to kill a woman or a hired worker."
"2107","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas bin Malik, who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, when he prayed the morning prayer during a journey, would walk a little away from his mount."
"2108","[AI-translation] Narrated from Jundub bin Sufyan that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was at one of the battlefields and his finger was bleeding, so he said: ""You are but a finger that bled, and what you suffered was in the path of Allah."
"2109","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn Abbas, Allah be pleased with him, marfu': The standard of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was white, and his banner was black."
"2110","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah bin Abu Awfa, who said: He used to prefer to advance against his enemy at the declining of the sun."
"2111","[AI-translation] Mughirah, from his grandfather Al-Mukhariq, who said: I met Ammar on the Day of the Camel while he was urinating in a horn. I said: ""Shall I fight with you and be with you?"" He said: ""Fight under the banner of your people, for the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, used to prefer for a man to fight under the banner of his people."
"2112","[AI-translation] Narrated from Umm Salamah, marfu': The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, used to prefer to travel on Thursday."
"2113","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, elevated: He used to train the horses and race them."
"2114","[AI-translation] Khattab, elevated: ""If I live, I will certainly expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula until I leave none but a Muslim."
"2115","[AI-translation] From 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from his father, he said: When Sa'd ibn Mu'adh gave judgment concerning Banu Qurayza that those on whom the blade passes be killed, and their wealth and progeny be divided, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""He has judged among them with the judgment of Allah that He judged from above seven heavens."
"2116","[AI-translation] From Hubayrah ibn Yarim, he said: I heard al-Hasan ibn 'Ali stand and address the people, saying: ""O people! Yesterday a man departed from you whom neither the predecessors surpassed nor will the successors attain. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, used to dispatch an expedition and give him the standard. He would not return until Allah granted him victory, with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left,"" meaning 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. ""He left neither white nor yellow, except for seven hundred dirhams that remained from his stipend, with which he intended to buy a servant."
"2117","[AI-translation] From 'Imran ibn Husayn, elevated: The standing of a man in a row in the path of Allah is better than the worship of sixty years."
"2118","[AI-translation] From Ibn Mas'ud: A man came with a haltered camel and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, this camel is in the path of Allah."" He said: ""For you are seven hundred haltered camels in Paradise."
"2119","[AI-translation] 'As, elevated: ""The warrior has his reward, and the one who equips him has his reward and the reward of the warrior."
"2120","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, elevated: Booty was not lawful for any of the black-headed ones before you. A fire used to descend from the sky and consume it. But on the day of Badr, they fell upon the booty before it was made lawful for them, so Allah revealed: ""Were it not for a decree from Allah that preceded, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took."" (Al-Anfal 68)"
"2121","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: ""Booty was not lawful for anyone before us. That is because Allah saw our weakness and inability, so He made it lawful for us."
"2122","[AI-translation] From Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, marched to Badr, he went out and consulted the people. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, advised him, then he consulted them, and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, advised him, but he remained silent. Then a man from the Ansar said, ""He only wants you."" They said, ""Are you consulting us, O Messenger of Allah?! By Allah, we will not say as the Children of Israel said to Musa, peace be upon him: 'Go, you and your Lord, and fight. Indeed, we are remaining right here.' (Al-Ma'idah) But by Allah, even if you struck the flanks of the camels until you reached Bark al-Ghimad, we would be with you."
"2123","[AI-translation] Darda' from the Prophet, peace be upon him: Were you forgiven for what you do to animals, you would be forgiven much."
"2124","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, raised to the Prophet: If people knew what I know about isolation, no rider would travel by night alone (ever)."
"2125","[AI-translation] From Umm Kabshah, a woman of Banu 'Udhrah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to go out with such and such army. He said: No. She said: O Prophet of Allah! I do not want to fight, I only want to treat the wounded and care for the sick. He said: Were it not that it would become a Sunnah, and it would be said, ""So-and-so went out,"" I would have permitted you. But sit in your house."
"2126","On the authority of Ya'la ibn Munyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) announced a military expedition, and I was an old man with no servant. So I sought a hired man to assist me, on the condition that I would give him his share of the spoils. I found a man, and when the departure drew near, he came to me and said: ""I do not know what the shares are, nor what my share will amount to; guarantee me something, whether there is a share or not."" So I stipulated three dinars for him. When the spoils were present, I intended to give him his share, but I remembered the dinars. So I went to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and informed him of the matter. He said: ""I find nothing for him in this expedition of his, in this world or the Hereafter, except the dinars he stipulated."""
"2127","[AI-translation] From Abu Bakr who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: No people abandon jihad except that Allah afflicts them with punishment."
"2128","[AI-translation] From Aisha: A mukatab of hers entered upon her with the remaining balance of his mukatabah, and she said to him: You shall not enter upon me after this visit of yours, so upon you be jihad in the path of Allah, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: No Muslim's heart is penetrated by the dust of battle in the path of Allah except that Allah makes the Fire forbidden for him."
"2129","[AI-translation] Samit that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: There is no soul on earth that dies, having good with Allah, that would love to return to you and have the world, except the slain (in the path of Allah), for he would love to return and be killed once more."
"2130","(2130) Habib ibn Shihab al-Anbari said: I heard my father say: I came to Ibn Abbas, I and a companion of mine, and we met Abu Hurayrah at the door of Ibn Abbas. He said: ""Who are you two?"" We informed him, and he said: ""Go to a people who have dates and water; each valley flows only according to its capacity."" We said: ""Much good is in you; seek permission for us to see Ibn Abbas."" So he sought permission for us, and we heard Ibn Abbas narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) delivered a sermon on the day of Tabuk and said: ""There is no one among the people like a man holding the reins of his horse, striving in the cause of Allah and avoiding the evils of people. And like a Bedouin man among his sheep, who hosts his guest and fulfills his right."" I said: ""Did he say that?"" He said: ""He said it."" I said: ""Did he say that?"" He said: ""He said it."" I said: ""Did he say that?"" He said: ""He said it."" So I magnified Allah, praised Allah, and thanked Him."
"2131","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas who said: ""And it is not for a prophet to act unfaithfully."" He said: It is not for a prophet that his companions should suspect him of unfaithfulness."
"2132","On the authority of Jarwal Zuhayr ibn Surad al-Jushami, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took us captive on the day of Hunayn—the day of Hawazin—and proceeded to distribute the young men and captives, I recited this poetry to him:""Bestow your favor upon us, O Messenger of Allah, in generosity,For you are the man we hope for and await.Bestow favor upon a people whom fate has afflicted,Their unity scattered, their fortunes changed by time.Time has left them crying out in grief,Upon their hearts are gloom and overwhelming sorrow.If your bounty does not reach them, spreading its grace,O most forbearing of people when tested.Bestow favor upon women who once nursed you,When your every action and inaction adorned you.Do not make them like one whose honor has been stripped away,So preserve us, for we are a noble people.We indeed give thanks for blessings when they are denied,And we have stored up [good deeds] after this day.So clothe with pardon those whom you once nursed,From your mothers, for pardon is well-known.O best of those whom noble steeds pranced beneath,At the onset of battle when sparks of war ignite.We hope for a pardon from you that we may wear,O guide of creation, when you pardon and prevail.So pardon, and may Allah pardon what you dread,On the Day of Resurrection when victory is granted to you.""When he heard this poetry, he said: ""What was mine and belongs to the Banu Abd al-Muttalib is yours."" Quraysh said: ""What was ours is for Allah and His Messenger."" And the Ansar said: ""What was ours is for Allah and His Messenger."""
"2133","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, who said: There is no human being except that in his head is a rein in the hand of an angel. When he humbles himself, it is said to the angel: Raise his rein. And when he acts arrogantly, it is said to the angel: Lower his rein."
"2134","[AI-translation] Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: There is no man who is wounded in his body with a wound and gives it in charity, except that Allah expiates for him the like of what he gave in charity."
"2135","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: The martyr feels nothing from the touch of killing except as one of you feels from the touch of a pinch."
"2136","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: The likeness of the one who strives in the path of Allah is like the fasting, standing, enduring one who does not cease from prayer or fasting until he returns."
"2137","[AI-translation] From 'Adiyy bin Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Al-Hirah was shown to me as if it were the fangs of dogs, and you will conquer it."" So a man stood up and said: ""Grant me the daughter of Buqaylah, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""She is yours."" So they gave her to him. Her father came and said: ""Will you sell her to me?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""For how much?"" He said: ""Set whatever price you wish."" He said: ""For a thousand dirhams."" He said: ""I have taken her."" It was said to him: ""If only you had said thirty thousand."" He said: ""Is there a number greater than a thousand?"
"2138","[AI-translation] Rabi' who said: I came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and he ordered for me a portion of camels. He said to me: ""Command your sons to trim their fingernails away from the udders of their camels and livestock, and say to them: let them milk over its young ones so that the year does not overtake them while they are emaciated."" He said: ""Do you have any wealth?"" I said: ""Yes, I have wealth, horses, and slaves."" He said: ""Upon you is the horse, so keep them, for in their forelocks is tied good."
"2139","[AI-translation] From 'Ali who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said to me and to Abu Bakr on the day of Badr: ""With one of you is Jibril, and with the other is Mika'il and Israfil, a great angel who witnesses the fighting."" Or he said: ""witnesses the row."
"2140","[AI-translation] That a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, passed by a mountain pass in which there was a spring of sweet water, and its pleasantness amazed him. He said: ""If only I could stay in this mountain pass and isolate myself from the people,"" but he said, ""I will not do it until I consult the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family."" So he mentioned that to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and he said: ""Do not do it, for the standing of one of you in the path of Allah is better than sixty years of prayer in isolation. Do you not love that Allah forgive you and enter you into Paradise? Campaign in the path of Allah; whoever fights in the path of Allah for the milking of a camel, Paradise is obligated for him."
"2141","[AI-translation] Anmari that a man came to him and said: ""Lend me your stallion, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Whoever lends his stallion to a Muslim will have the like of the reward of seventy horses ridden in the path of Allah. And if it is not restrained, it will be for him like ??? horses ridden in the path of Allah."
"2142","[AI-translation] From 'Abayah bin Rifa'ah who said: Abu 'Abs caught up with me while I was going to Jumu'ah and said: ""Rejoice, for these footsteps of yours are in the path of Allah."" I heard him, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Whosever feet become dusty in the path of Allah, Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"2143","[AI-translation] From Mu'adh bin Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection with his scent being the scent of musk and his color the color of saffron, upon him being the seal of the martyrs. And whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely, Allah will grant him the reward of a martyr even if he dies in his bed."
"2144","[AI-translation] Juhani, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah, he has the like of his reward, and whoever stays behind a warrior in the path of Allah regarding his family with good, and spends (on his family), he has the like of his reward."
"2145","[AI-translation] From Zayd bin Thabit, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah, he has the like of his reward, and whoever stays behind a warrior regarding his family with good, or spends on his family, he has the like of his reward."
"2146","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever goes out for Hajj and dies, Allah will write for him the reward of a pilgrim until the Day of Resurrection. And whoever goes out for Umrah and dies, Allah will write for him the reward of one performing Umrah until the Day of Resurrection. And whoever goes out as a fighter in the cause of Allah and dies, Allah will write for him the reward of a fighter until the Day of Resurrection."
"2147","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever goes out in the morning in the cause of Allah, whatever dust afflicts him will be like musk for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"2148","[AI-translation] Ansari: ""Whoever is turned back by omens has committed Shirk."
"2149","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever shoots an arrow in the cause of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"2150","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, elevated to the Prophet: ""Whoever shoots at us at night is not of us."
"2151","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, he said: ... I said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Which of the martyrs is best?"" He said: ""The one whose blood is shed and whose steed is hamstrung."
"2152","[AI-translation] From Uqbah bin 'Amir, elevated to the Prophet: ""Whoever is thrown from his mount in the cause of Allah, he is a martyr."
"2153","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Abd Allah, from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, on a journey, and he went to attend to his need, and we saw a bird with two chicks, so we took its chicks. The bird came and began to flutter its wings. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, came and said: ""Who has bereaved this of its child? Return its child to it."" And he saw an ant village which we had burned, so he said: ""Who burned this?"" We said: ""We did."" He said: ""None should punish with the fire except the Lord of the Fire."
"2154","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, he said: ""Whoever does not go out for military expedition, nor equip a fighter, nor take care of a fighter's family with good, Allah, the Exalted, will strike him with a calamity before the Day of Resurrection."
"2155","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, that he was in Ribat, and they were alarmed, so they went out to the coast. Then it was said: ""No harm,"" so the people departed, while Abu Hurayrah was standing. A person passed by him and said: ""What makes you stand here, O Abu Hurayrah?"" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: 'Standing for an hour in the cause of Allah is better than standing on the Night of Decree by the Black Stone.'"
"2156","[AI-translation] On the authority of Anas, raising it: ""Victory is with patience, relief is with distress, and that with hardship comes ease, and that with hardship comes ease."
"2157","[AI-translation] Zubayr ibn Al-Awwam, he said: Khalid ibn Hizam migrated to the land of Abyssinia, but a snake bit him on the way and he died. So it was revealed concerning him. Al-Zubayr ibn Al-Awwam said: ""I was expecting him and awaiting his arrival while I was in the land of Abyssinia. Nothing saddened me as much as my sorrow over missing him when the news reached me, because hardly anyone from Quraysh migrated except with some of his family or a relative, and there was no one from Banu Asad ibn Abd Al-Uzza with me, nor did I expect anyone else."
"2158","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ka'b ibn Malik, he used to narrate that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, it is as if you shoot them with arrows regarding what you say to them of poetry."
"2159","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, a young man appeared from the mountain pass. When we cast our gaze upon him, we said: ""If only this young man would devote his energy, his youth, and his strength in the path of Allah."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, heard our words and said: ""And is the path of Allah only for those who are killed? Whoever strives for his parents is in the path of Allah, and whoever strives for his dependents is in the path of Allah, (and whoever strives for himself to keep chaste is in the path of Allah), and whoever strives out of boasting is in the path of Taghut."" And in a narration: ""In the path of Satan."
"2160","[AI-translation] On the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The people must have an 'Arif, and the 'Arif is in the Fire."
"2161","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Abbas was traveling with the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, on a camel that he had branded on its face with fire. He said: ""What is this brand, O Abbas?"" He said: ""A brand we used to apply in the pre-Islamic days."" He said: ""Do not brand with the burning."
"2162","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Musa, he said: I was with Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, and a caravan belonging to Umm Al-Banin passed by, in which were bells. Salim narrated from his father, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, that he said: ""The angels do not accompany a riding party that has a bell with them."" He said: ""So how many bells do you see among these?!"
"2163","[AI-translation] On the authority of Yahya ibn Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, that when the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, sent Ali, he sent a man behind him. He said: ""Follow Ali, and do not leave him behind you, but follow him and take him by his hand, and say to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, says: Stay until he comes to you."" He said: So he stayed until the Prophet, peace be upon him, came, and he said: ""Do not fight a people until you call them."
"2164","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abdullah ibn Rawahah, that he was with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, during a journey. He said: ""O Ibn Rawahah, dismount and move the riding beast."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I have left that."" Umar said: ""Listen and obey."" He said: So he threw himself down and said: ""O Allah, were it not for You we would not have been guided, nor would we have given charity, nor would we have prayed. So send down tranquility upon us, and make our feet firm if we meet them."
"2165","[AI-translation] On the authority of Anas, that Umm Sulaym was with Abu Talhah on the day of Hunayn. She had a dagger with her. Abu Talhah said: ""What is this with you, O Umm Sulaym?"" She said: ""I took it so that if any of the disbelievers comes near me, I will slit his belly with it."" Abu Talhah said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Do you not hear what Umm Sulaym is saying? She says such and such."" He (Anas) said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Kill those behind us from the Tulaqa; they have fled, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""O Umm Sulaym, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has sufficed us and been gracious."
"2166","On the authority of Umm Salamah: That Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) emigrated, sought permission from her husband Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi' to go to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so he gave her permission and she came to him. Then Abu al-As caught up with her in Medina and sent word to her saying: ""Seek protection for me from your father."" So she went out and poked her head out from the door of her chamber while the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was leading the people in the morning prayer. She said: ""O people! I am Zaynab bint Muhammad, and I have granted protection to Abu al-As."" When the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: ""O people! I did not know about this until I heard it from you. Verily, the protection granted by the lowest of the Muslims is binding upon all Muslims."""
"2167","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to me: ""O Jabir! Did you not know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brought your father back to life and said to him: 'Ask of Me.' He said: 'I wish to be returned to the world so that I may be killed again.' He said: 'Indeed, I have decreed the judgment that they shall not return to it.'"
"2168","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Abdullah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""O Jadd! Would you like to fight Banu al-Asfar?"" Jadd said: ""Do you permit me, O Messenger of Allah? For I am a man who loves women, and I fear that if I see the daughters of Banu al-Asfar, I will be tempted."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said while turning away from him: ""I have permitted you."" At that, Allah revealed: ""And among them is he who says, 'Permit me and do not put me to trial.' Unquestionably, they have fallen into trial."" [At-Tawbah: 49]"
